{"parentUuid":"8c3be569-9398-4044-9715-e8cefc6ca015","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZa4Lc6nvf7U6qtabgBc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build turn is still running, at step 7 of its tool calls. The background watcher will report when it finishes.\n\nDone so far in this stretch:\n- **The plan is rewritten around your two points** (`c963b33`):\n  - **Definitions:** charter (a project's own rules, or none), harness, and factory (Bastion is both).\n  - **Ladders:** constraints are told, checked, or enforced; capabilities are denied, ask, or allowed. Each can be promoted or demoted.\n  - **Goals and decisions:** goals 10–12, plus decisions D20 (rules as hooks), D21 (a tamper-evident hash-chain audit), D22 (A/B evals of harness configurations), and D23 (forge, tracker, CI, providers, and notifications as adapters you choose in Settings).\n  - **New phase order:** A4 review and landing, A5 constraints, capabilities and the audit, A6 A/B evals, A7 settings and integrations, A8 the full pipeline, then operations, learning, the browser agent, notifications, and packaging.\n- **A4 step 1, the diff** (`e5da6d7`): captured from the VM when a build finishes, shown per file with line numbers, and clicking a line starts a `file:line:` comment. This works live.\n- **A4 step 2, the checkpoint dial** (`0bdb745`): ask, hold, or auto for each checkpoint, with Review never below hold. Holds resume after a restart, and the dial is set in Settings. It is covered by 23 core tests, but I have not checked it live; a hold takes 30 minutes to run out.\n\n**What the live run found, and the fixes (not yet committed):**\n- The agent's report said it added a docstring and committed, but the diff showed neither. The VM had the fix uncommitted. The review now lists uncommitted files under \"Not committed, so it will not land\".\n- Turns failed on VM tool calls without a `sandbox_id`. Each turn now gets a tool guide that uses a placeholder id, which the hook replaces.\n- gpt-5-mini ended turns by announcing its next step (\"I will run …\"). The guide now tells it that its reply ends the turn.\n\nThese are the kind of behaviors A5's constraints should enforce, and A6's evals should measure. One example: \"a build leaves a clean tree\" as a checked constraint.\n\n**Still open in A4:** this rebuild's result, then approving and landing `divide` into `demo-b`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":852690,"output_tokens":897,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":92},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":852690,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8016128f-c791-4754-a3c5-f5be10a65641","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZa4LEnCJ2cJqG9qTSfo","type":"assistant","uuid":"c6f6ffa1-64c5-4404-88f3-68bee4e4b059","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:02:33.194Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
